  "result": "**Ruling 3 recorded.** The project has no decision register or handoff file, so here it is in one line: \"Cut over `SMTP_RELAY` from `smtp-old-1` to `smtp-mx-2` on 14 November.\"\n\nNo open item remains. The cutover lands 16 days before `smtp-old-1` goes offline on 30 November. The month-end invoice run on 30 November will therefore go through `smtp-mx-2`.\n\n**Next step.** Aelita implements the three rulings together in `mailer/config.py` and `mailer/bounces.py`, ready to deploy on 14 November:\n\n- `mailer/config.py`: `SMTP_RELAY` becomes `smtp-mx-2.larkspur.internal`. `FROM_ADDRESS` becomes `invoices@mail.larkspur.io`. `BOUNCE_RETRY_LIMIT` falls from 12 to 3. `BOUNCE_RETRY_INTERVAL_SECONDS` rises from 60 to 1200.\n- `mailer/bounces.py`: `handle_bounce` tells hard bounces from soft bounces. It calls `message.mark_failed()` at once on a hard bounce and never retries.\n\nA recipient then bounces at most 4 times in one hour: the first send plus 3 retries. That stays under the `smtp-mx-2` block threshold of more than 5.",
